{"availability":"available","full":"danja/jigdaw","name":"jigdaw","description":"Web-based music plugin system","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":5,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-16T16:53:21Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:30:00Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://danja.github.io/jigdaw/","topics":["daw","music","plugins"],"demo":"https://danja.github.io/jigdaw/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.160Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.160Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.160Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.160Z","stars":5,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Jig is a plugin conforming to this specification.","A plugin is a dereferenceable IRI. Fetching it is installing it. What comes back says what the plugin is, what signals it accepts and produces, what it needs from a host, and where its WebAssembly module, its AudioWorklet processor and its user interface are, each with an integrity digest. There is no registry, and no install step distinct from having fetched it.","The rest of this repository exists to support the specification: a host that runs the plugins in a browser, a second host that runs them as a VST3, 32 worked plugins, and a validator that enforces the specification on its own files."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/danja/jigdaw/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"274931f64cdc7a1b22ceb44b2610cfeb75ede88a455333567a2f944909720efc","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.395Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.395Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Jig is a plugin conforming to this specification.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/danja/jigdaw/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"274931f64cdc7a1b22ceb44b2610cfeb75ede88a455333567a2f944909720efc","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/danja/jigdaw/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:26.395